  {
    "id": "digital-r2-A-Synthesis",
    "contentSha256": "9d6cc1f9af6ec6980b2adeaa764afa4c5e4f9a4c42bb025533707cfd5f6cabfc",
    "brandMentions": [
      {
        "line": 12,
        "text": "Keep the story on the documented sequencing and cadence: applicants came first, then the team used a defined rhythm to develop and research the service while processing applications. Explain this as Nuëyon’s account of one product’s direction and working choices, not as advice or a universal recipe for service design. The five-week figures may be used as reported context, but not as proof that these choices caused the results."
      }
    ],
